      "nets": ["+5V", "I2C_SDA", "I2C_SCL"],
      "observed": "In the 'Water Height Sensor' block (page 1, sheet 1/1), the TF-Luna LiDAR PR1 is wired through connector H1 to the +5V rail and to the global labels I2C_SDA and I2C_SCL, i.e. PR1.VCC→+5V, PR1.SDA→I2C_SDA, PR1.SCL→I2C_SCL. The part carries no DNP/no-connect marker (unlike PR5/PR6).",
      "expected": "The specification states the LiDAR is not connected to any net and is excluded from the board: 'the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no, in_bom: yes, and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design' and 'TF-Luna LiDAR is unwired: ... its pins are typed free, it is marked on_board: no, and it has no corresponding firmware code.' The intended water-level path is the float switches / ultrasonic sensor, not a wired LiDAR.",
