        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PR1 with on_board: no ... all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "TF-Luna LiDAR is unwired: ... it is marked on_board: no, and it has no corresponding firmware code"}
      ],
      "impact": "A device the intended design deliberately leaves disconnected is now an active load on the +5V rail and on the main I2C bus. It draws quiescent current and presents an uncommanded I2C slave that firmware never initializes or reads, which can load/disturb the shared I2C bus and contradicts the documented non-implementation of the LiDAR.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic deviates from the intended design by wiring the TF-Luna LiDAR (PR1) to the +5V rail and the main I2C bus (I2C_SDA/I2C_SCL), whereas the specification repeatedly states PR1's pins are free and it is not connected to any net (on_board: no); this adds an uncommanded device and load to the bus."
}

